  "limitations": [
    "The research has not studied the difference between the response to different colours and light intensities based on gender and age.",
    "The direction of change in HR (increase or decrease) is subject dependent, which makes it hard to correlate the colour and lighting condition to a specific effect on HR.",
    "HR is not a good measure when considering the effect of a stimulus on a group of people because the HR of individuals is very different."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This empirical study investigated the physiological effects of different color and light conditions on human heart rate (HR). Findings indicate that while color and light exposure for 10 minutes significantly changes individuals' HR, the direction of this change (increase or decrease) is highly subject-dependent. Consequently, HR was not found to be a statistically significant measure for the average response of a group to color and light, suggesting high inter-subject variability. Limitations include not studying gender and age differences, and the difficulty in correlating specific color/light conditions to a consistent HR effect due to individual variability.",
